   ("Sulphate tests", ["Sulphate ions give a white precipitate of barium sulphate with barium chloride solution (insoluble in dilute HCl). Sulphites and hydrogen sulphide are also tested — H2S has a rotten-egg smell and gives a black precipitate of lead sulphide with lead nitrate."]),
