   ("Air and the greenhouse effect", ["Clean dry air: 78% nitrogen, 21% oxygen, about 1% argon, 0.04% carbon dioxide, with traces of other gases, water vapour and dust. CO2 and water vapour (and methane) are greenhouse gases: they trap outgoing heat, keeping the earth warm. The burning of fossil fuels has raised CO2 levels — the enhanced greenhouse effect warming the planet, melting glaciers and raising sea levels."]),
